## sn45.30
sn45.30:1.1 | S: At Sāvatthī. | T: At Savatthī.
sn45.30:1.2 | S: Then Venerable Uttiya went up to the Buddha … and asked him, | T: Then the Venerable Uttiya approached the Blessed One … and said to him:
sn45.30:1.3 | S: “Just now, sir, as I was in private retreat this thought came to mind. | T: “Here, venerable sir, when I was alone in seclusion a reflection arose in my mind thus:
sn45.30:1.4 | S: ‘The Buddha has spoken of the five kinds of sensual stimulation. | T: ‘Five cords of sensual pleasure have been spoken of by the Blessed One.
sn45.30:1.5 | S: What are they?’” | T: But what now are those five cords of sensual pleasure?’”
sn45.30:1.6 | S: “Good, good, Uttiya! | T: “Good, good, Uttiya!
sn45.30:1.7 | S: I have spoken of these five kinds of sensual stimulation. | T: These five cords of sensual pleasure have been spoken of by me.
sn45.30:1.8 | S: What five? | T: What five?
sn45.30:1.9 | S: Sights known by the eye, which are likable, desirable, agreeable, pleasant, sensual, and arousing. | T: Forms cognizable by the eye that are desirable, lovely, agreeable, pleasing, sensually enticing, tantalizing.
sn45.30:1.10 | S: Sounds known by the ear … | T: Sounds cognizable by the ear …
sn45.30:1.11 | S: Smells known by the nose … | T: Odours cognizable by the nose …
sn45.30:1.12 | S: Tastes known by the tongue … | T: Tastes cognizable by the tongue …
sn45.30:1.13 | S: Touches known by the body, which are likable, desirable, agreeable, pleasant, sensual, and arousing. | T: Tactile objects cognizable by the body that are desirable, lovely, agreeable, pleasing, sensually enticing, tantalizing.
sn45.30:1.14 | S: These are the five kinds of sensual stimulation that I’ve spoken of. | T: These are the five cords of sensual pleasure spoken of by me.
sn45.30:1.15 | S: The noble eightfold path should be developed to give up these five kinds of sensual stimulation. | T: “The Noble Eightfold Path, Uttiya, is to be developed for the abandoning of these five cords of sensual pleasure.
sn45.30:1.16 | S: What is the noble eightfold path? | T: And what is the Noble Eightfold Path?
sn45.30:1.17 | S: It is right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion. | T: It is: right view … right concentration.
sn45.30:1.18 | S: This is the noble eightfold path that should be developed to give up these five kinds of sensual stimulation.” | T: This Noble Eightfold Path is to be developed for the abandoning of these five cords of sensual pleasure.”
