## sn45.41
sn45.41:1.1 | S: At Sāvatthī. | T: At Savatthī.
sn45.41:1.2 | S: “Mendicants, if wanderers who follow another religion were to ask you: | T: “Bhikkhus, if wanderers of other sects ask you:
sn45.41:1.3 | S: ‘Reverends, what’s the goal of leading the spiritual life under the ascetic Gotama?’ You should answer them like this: | T: ‘For what purpose, friends, is the holy life lived under the ascetic Gotama?’—being asked thus, you should answer them thus:
sn45.41:1.4 | S: ‘The goal of leading the spiritual life under the Buddha is the fading away of greed.’ | T: ‘It is, friends, for the fading away of lust that the holy life is lived under the Blessed One.’
sn45.41:1.5 | S: If wanderers of other religions were to ask you: | T: “Then, bhikkhus, if the wanderers of other sects ask you:
sn45.41:1.6 | S: ‘Is there a path and a practice for the fading away of greed?’ You should answer them like this: | T: ‘But, friends, is there a path, is there a way for the fading away of lust?’—being asked thus, you should answer them thus:
sn45.41:1.7 | S: ‘There is a path and a practice for the fading away of greed.’ | T: ‘There is a path, friends, there is a way for the fading away of lust.’
sn45.41:1.8 | S: And what is that path, what is that practice for the fading away of greed? | T: “And what, bhikkhus, is that path, what is that way for the fading away of lust?
sn45.41:1.9 | S: It is simply this noble eightfold path, that is: | T: It is this Noble Eightfold Path; that is,
sn45.41:1.10 | S: right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion. | T: right view … right concentration.
sn45.41:1.11 | S: This is the path, this is the practice for the fading away of greed. | T: This is the path, this is the way for the fading away of lust.
sn45.41:1.12 | S: When questioned by wanderers of other religions, that’s how you should answer them.” | T: “Being asked thus, bhikkhus, you should answer those wanderers of other sects in such a way.”
sn45.41:1.13 | P: Paṭhamaṁ. | T: (none)

## sn45.42-47
sn45.42-47:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, if wanderers who follow another religion were to ask you: | T: “Bhikkhus, if wanderers of other sects ask you:
