## sn45.6
sn45.6:1.1 | S: At Sāvatthī. | T: At Savatthī.
sn45.6:1.2 | S: Then a mendicant went up to the Buddha … and asked him, | T: Then a certain bhikkhu approached the Blessed One…. Sitting to one side, that bhikkhu said to the Blessed One:
sn45.6:1.3 | S: “Sir, they speak of this thing called the ‘spiritual path’. | T: “Venerable sir, it is said, ‘the holy life, the holy life.’
sn45.6:1.4 | S: What is the spiritual path? And what is the culmination of the spiritual path?” | T: What, venerable sir, is the holy life? What is the final goal of the holy life?”
sn45.6:2.1 | S: “Mendicant, the spiritual path is simply this noble eightfold path, that is: | T: “This Noble Eightfold Path, bhikkhu, is the holy life; that is,
sn45.6:2.2 | S: right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion. | T: right view … right concentration.
sn45.6:2.3 | S: The ending of greed, hate, and delusion. | T: The destruction of lust, the destruction of hatred, the destruction of delusion:
sn45.6:2.4 | S: This is the culmination of the spiritual path.” | T: this is the final goal of the holy life.”
sn45.6:2.5 | P: Chaṭṭhaṁ. | T: (none)

